    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the file `stream_microphone.py` that streams microphone audio and yields interim transcripts, I need to integrate with a concrete external provider. Google Cloud Speech-to-Text API is a suitable choice for this task. I will use the `google-cloud-speech` Python client library to interact with the API. This library will be identifiable in the code through the import statement and the use of the client class specific to Google Cloud Speech-to-Text. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789889058319,
          "start": 1789889054624
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bdb387a0001YkGA6aU1VjP289",
      "message_id": "msg_0bdb381fb0014dXCtUjBp64p64",
      "session_id": "ses_f424c7e85ffeQX7i03D3PutNkv",
